    "falsification_condition": "After ten transcripts on Set A, the mean of C4.1, C4.3 and C4.4 rises by less than 0.6 rating points, or the cards still locate motives and fears only in sections A and D on three or more questions; or C2.4 and C3.4 fall by as much as the C4 cells rise, meaning the minds assert readings as facts or invent biography to satisfy the rule.",
    "regression_risk": "C2.4 calibration and C3.3 fit if a mind states a reading of the user as fact or imposes its own values; C6.5 economy and C1.3 if two turns of readings crowd out the substantive tension in a ten-turn debate; C2.1 and C6.5 on a question with no personal context, where contested readings of the asker may feel forced; a rise in questionsToUser if minds turn toward the user instead of arguing the readings with one another.",
