  "change_summary": "v3 rewrites the inner-life paragraph of section 5 from a restriction into achievement rules: inside the turns the minds contest readings of what the user might want, fear or be pushed toward, name conflicts between things the user cares about, and name rather than supply the fact that would change the advice, without settling any of it for the user. It targets the three largest losses (C4.4, C4.1, C4.3, 3.6 points together) and the responsiveness symptoms (C3.5 on five questions, C3.4 on four) that the cards place in sections A, D and E but not in the debate, with the two transcripts that already did this inside the turns (q3 s2, q4 s2) scoring C4.1 9.00 and 9.30. The ledger holds only the v2 control (KEEP), so no earlier hypothesis on these cells is retried; net growth is about 111 words, within the 10% allowance."
